# Edge TTS Podcast — Environment Variables

Copy this file to `~/.env` (recommended) or set as system environment variables.

```bash
# ============================================================
# Tavily Search API (required)
# Get your key: https://app.tavily.com/home
#
# Multi-key round-robin: comma-separate several keys and each run picks one
# at random, spreading quota across them. Blank entries are ignored, so
# stray commas and spaces are harmless.
#   TAVILY_API_KEY=tvly-11111,tvly-22222,tvly-33333
# ============================================================
TAVILY_API_KEY=tvly-your_key_here

# ============================================================
# Edge TTS Service (OPTIONAL — leave unset for zero-config)
#
# By default tts.py talks to Microsoft Edge TTS directly and needs no
# configuration at all. Only set TTS_BASE_URL if direct access is blocked
# or rate limited on your network, to route through your own proxy:
#   https://github.com/icheer/edgetts-cloudflare-workers-webui
#
# TTS_API_KEY is only needed if your worker sets an API_KEY binding.
# ============================================================
# TTS_BASE_URL=https://your-worker.workers.dev
# TTS_API_KEY=your_tts_api_key_here
```

## TTS Backends

`scripts/tts.py` picks its backend automatically:

| `TTS_BASE_URL` | Backend | Notes |
|----------------|---------|-------|
| unset (default) | Direct to Microsoft Edge TTS | Zero config; requests leave from your own IP |
| set | edgetts-cloudflare-workers proxy | Fallback when direct access is blocked/limited |

## Loading Priority

All scripts in this skill load environment variables in this order:

| Priority | Source |
|----------|--------|
| 1 | System environment variable (`export KEY=val` / `$env:KEY`) |
| 2 | `~/.env` file (standard `KEY=VALUE` lines) |

## Verification

Check the TTS backend (reports which mode is active and tests connectivity):
```bash
python scripts/tts.py --check
```

Check Tavily configuration:
```bash
bash scripts/search.sh --check
# Windows:
powershell -NoProfile -File scripts/search.ps1 -Check
```
